    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0644" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.73/210: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-07T17:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date>]<lb/>[Received 6:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Department’s 10, February 4, 4 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="44" xml:id="d262-f1"/> Western Telegraph representative sent me this
                    afternoon copy of petition presented today to the Brazilian Government and
                    addressed to the Director General of Telegraphs in the Ministry of Public Works
                    containing copy of Secretary’s telegram covering resolution of Western relative
                    to preferential and exclusive rights for the operation of all submarine cables
                    in South America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
